-- title:
--   Branch ideals at a crossing meet in (p)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \geq 1$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \leq (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$, and assume $M/p \neq 0$; assume the $q$-series $j$, `jqModC ℚ`, lies in the subfield `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the integral-form ratios for $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be Deligne–Rapoport model data `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for $X_H(M)$ over `R p`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, with residue field of characteristic $p$ and algebraically closed, and $\rho :$ `R p` $\to A$ a ring map compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal $(p)$, $\rho_O :$ `R p` $\to O$, and $t : O \to \kappa_A$ with $t \circ \rho_O$ equal to the residue map composed after $\rho$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` presenting the components of the geometric special fibre, and $x_n =$ `𝔛.crossingPt … n` its image in $X_O =$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, namely the image of $n$ under the base map of the first projection followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by `bcMap`. Assume the points `𝔛.ξinf …` and `𝔛.ξzero …` of $X_O$ both specialise to $x_n$. Then in $\mathcal{O}_{X_O,x_n}$ the intersection of the two branch ideals, each being the preimage of the maximal ideal of the stalk at `𝔛.ξinf …` resp. `𝔛.ξzero …` under the corresponding specialisation map of stalks, equals the principal ideal generated by the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of $X_O$ obtained from $p \in O$ along the structure morphism `XO.toBase`.
--
--   This records that near a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over $O$, the fibre $X_O \otimes O/(p)$ is exactly the union of the two branches through that point: the two branch ideals intersect in the ideal generated by the uniformiser $p$. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal) and, through it, to the construction of oriented étale crossing charts of the form $xy = p$ in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart).
